\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Cyclic proof graph for reverse-append fusion. The standard SC gets stuck at the cons branch (red); the LLM proposes a lemma (green) that rewrites the stuck configuration into a form that folds (blue backlink) to the root. Without the lemma, standard SC produces different residuals for the two sides of the equation; with the lemma, the residuals are identical. }}{10}{figure.1.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:reverse-append-graph}{{1}{10}{Cyclic proof graph for reverse-append fusion. The standard SC gets stuck at the cons branch (red); the LLM proposes a lemma (green) that rewrites the stuck configuration into a form that folds (blue backlink) to the root. Without the lemma, standard SC produces different residuals for the two sides of the equation; with the lemma, the residuals are identical}{figure.1.1}{}}
